WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.080
- How are you?

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:01.913
- I'm good, thank you.

00:00:01.913 --> 00:00:02.746
- [Kelly] You're good?

00:00:02.746 --> 00:00:03.579
- How are you?

00:00:03.579 --> 00:00:04.412
- I know there was like, a health scare.

00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:05.245
You're good though, right?

00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:06.078
- Um, yes.

00:00:06.078 --> 00:00:06.911
There was a health scare,

00:00:06.911 --> 00:00:07.800
I'm totally okay now.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.180
I'm doing much better.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.800
I'm doing completely fine.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.210
- And it was something random, right?

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.410
That you'd never heard of.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.330
I think that's, it's not cool
that it's happening to you,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.163
but I think that it's cool

00:00:16.163 --> 00:00:16.996
that you're putting a spotlight on it

00:00:16.996 --> 00:00:18.120
for people that maybe didn't
have the spotlight on it.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.300
- Yeah, it was something that,
honestly, I was born with.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.670
I was born with a heart
defect, it's called a PFO.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.950
I won't try to butcher the
actual name of it, but.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:26.783
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:28.440
- Basically I was born
with a hole in my heart

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.490
and it never closed.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.677
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:31.510
- And I didn't know.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.343
Apparently it's very, very common.

00:00:32.343 --> 00:00:34.290
A lot of people have
it and they don't know.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.790
Um, and it was just kind of like

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.955
this perfect storm of
things that led to me

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:41.070
having a small blood clot,

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.440
which was really scary and really crazy.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.330
And I had something called a TIA,

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.370
which is like a mini stroke.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.203
- Geez.

00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:49.036
- [Hailey] Yeah.

00:00:49.036 --> 00:00:50.010
- And you're so young, but it's like,

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.240
it's horrible that it happened to you,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.800
but it's nice that you're
putting awareness on it

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:53.633
just for people.

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:54.466
- [Hailey] Yeah.

00:00:54.466 --> 00:00:56.100
- 'Cause can you get like a
scan to check that, to see?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:56.933
- Um, you-

00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:57.766
- 'Cause I've had a heart scan,

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:58.599
I don't know if they could tell me

00:00:58.599 --> 00:00:59.432
if there was a hole in it.

00:00:59.432 --> 00:01:00.420
- You can, there's a
special type of testing

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.253
you can do for it.

00:01:01.253 --> 00:01:02.730
And I never knew any of this before.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.890
I thought I was 25 and healthy.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:05.723
- Well you're like, young.

00:01:05.723 --> 00:01:07.389
Like why? Yeah, like
I wouldn't have, yeah.

00:01:07.389 --> 00:01:08.222
- I had no idea,

00:01:08.222 --> 00:01:10.710
but it's been a big learning experience.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.540
I, you know, I made a video about it,

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.650
I talked about everything,

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.900
and hopefully it can help someone

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:16.980
going through the same thing, so.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:17.850
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.020
And just something to be aware of

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:19.853
'cause I'd never heard of that.

00:01:19.853 --> 00:01:20.686
- Yeah.

